WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.609
The European Space Agency's Sentinel-1 radar
satellites image the global ocean at unprecedented scale,

00:00:06.689 --> 00:00:10.478
capturing waves, turbulence, fronts, and biological
slicks.

00:00:10.558 --> 00:00:13.167
Computer vision can process these images,

00:00:13.247 --> 00:00:17.495
but machine learning has been held back by a lack
of labeled data,

00:00:17.575 --> 00:00:21.167
since only trained experts can annotate radar vignettes.

00:00:21.247 --> 00:00:28.709
Earlier work also relied on a biased dataset that
picked only exemplary images and forced a single label per image,

00:00:28.789 --> 00:00:31.791
even though multiple phenomena usually coexist.

00:00:31.871 --> 00:00:37.890
The result was a training set that did not reflect
the real distribution of ocean conditions.
